cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Nieuwland numbers of 175 convex polyhedra, proved in Lean"
authors:
  - family-names: Hervay
    given-names: Bence
version: "1.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24564757
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/bence-hervay/nopert-nieuwland-lean"
url: "https://bence.io/nieuwland-explorer/"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 proofs, built on Mathlib, that decide Rupertness for 175 convex polyhedra (151 Rupert,
  24 Noperts) and give each its exact Nieuwland number: all 5 Platonic, 13 Archimedean,
  13 Catalan, and 92 Johnson solids, prisms, antiprisms, their duals, nine triakis tetrahedra,
  and seven others. For each Rupert solid, Lean proves that the Nieuwland number is the only
  root of a rational polynomial system in a rational box, that a pose given by the same root
  fits weakly at that scale, and that no larger copy fits. With an interactive explorer.
keywords:
  - Rupert's problem
  - Rupert property
  - Nopert
  - Nieuwland number
  - convex polyhedra
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
